    "summary": "High‑energy Hawaiian set with stellar Dark Star and tight jams",
    "blurb": "The show bursts with a soaring China Cat Sunflower → Rider segue, a monster Dark Star into Saint Stephen, and an inspired Turn On Your Lovelight. Jerry’s guitar is on fire while the rhythm section drives the extended Good Lovin' / The Other One jams. Overall the performance is tight, energetic and captures the 1970 vibe.",
    "review": "On January 23, 1970 at Honolulu Civic Auditorium the Dead delivered a blistering set that still feels fresh decades later. Opening with a bright China Cat Sunflower that glides straight into I Know You Rider, the band kept the momentum rolling into Black Peter before slipping into a gritty Hard To Handle that exposed a few lyrical hiccups. The second half truly shines: an extended Good Lovin' jam folds seamlessly into Cryptical Envelopment, then erupts through The Other One and another round of Cryptical, launching into a monumental Dark Star that rides all the way into Saint Stephen before bursting out into a joyous Turn On Your Lovelight. Jerry’s hot slide work and soaring leads dominate the highlights, while Bob’s vocal swagger adds humor and character. The twin‑drum engine of Mickey and Bill stays rock‑solid, propelling the improvisations with tight, driving pulse. With crisp soundboard capture that balances each instrument, this performance stands out as one of the band’s most vibrant early‑70s outings.",
